What the MIT License above covers, and what it does not

The MIT License covers the code in this repository: scripts/, tools/,
templates/, assets-src/, the tests in tests/ (not tests/fixtures/, see below),
every script and stylesheet in site/ (app.js, 404.js, style.css, 404.css,
print.css, party.css), site/404.html, site/legacy-map.json and the
configuration files.

It does not cover the following, which keep their own terms:

- The WiiVolve name and the site's own text (the hero, About and deep-end
  copy). Copyright (c) 2026 Ali Kurnaz. All rights reserved.

- The original 2006-2008 WiiVolve material: the archived headlines in
  site/archive.json, the recovered header art in site/legacy/ and everything
  in legacy-assets/. It was written by the WiiVolve staff of 2006-2008 (Ali
  Kurnaz and contributors; legacy-assets/FACTS.md lists the bylines), whose
  rights it keeps, and in places it quoted or reprinted other publications,
  as the archived pages say.

- The saved feeds in tests/fixtures/ (the .xml files): copies of public RSS
  and Atom feeds, copyright their publishers, kept only to test the parser.

- The Bricolage Grotesque font (site/fonts/bricolage-grotesque-96.woff2),
  Copyright 2022 The Bricolage Grotesque Project Authors, licensed under the
  SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. See site/fonts/OFL.txt.

- The headlines, excerpts and links in the generated news files
  (site/index.html, site/news.json, site/feed.xml, site/feed.json), which
  belong to their publishers. WiiVolve only links to them.

WiiVolve is not affiliated with or endorsed by Nintendo. Wii and the names of
Nintendo products are trademarks of Nintendo.
